%S A398565 1,3,27,2187,14348907,617673396283947,1144561273430837494885949696427,
%T A398565 3930061525912861057173624287137506221892737197425280369698987
%N A398565 a(n) = 3^(2^n - 1).
%C A398565 a(n) is also the number of distinct subdivisions of a triangle after n iterations of median division (when at each iteration, for every triangle, one of the three median line segments is selected, splitting the chosen triangle into two new triangles).
%H A398565 Jos Vromans, <a href="https://www.josvromans.art/writing/2021/1/triangle-subdivisions/">Triangle Subdivisions</a>
%H A398565 Jos Vromans, <a href="https://archief.vakbladeuclides.nl/bestanden/098_2022-23_03.pdf">Symmetrische Driehoeksverdelingen</a>, Euclides, 98 (3) (2022), 14-17. (Full journal in Dutch)
%F A398565 a(n) = 3^(2^n - 1).
%F A398565 a(n) = 3^A000225(n).
%p A398565 a := n -> 3^((2^n) - 1);
%t A398565 a[n_] := 3^((2^n) - 1)
%o A398565 (Python) def a(n):return 3**(2**n-1)
%Y A398565 Cf. A000225.
%K A398565 nonn,easy,new
%O A398565 0,2
